  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 28f310e05cc019a48855581da30b411e, type: 3}
  m_Name: AdoboHistory
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lines:
  - text: Pork Adobo! But there's an interesting question behind this familiar favorite
      where did adobo really begin?
    characterSprite: {fileID: -511706578061346315, guid: ae71825725b21a3459805439433622ee, type: 3}
  - text: Let me tell you the history and origin of adobo.
    characterSprite: {fileID: -511706578061346315, guid: ae71825725b21a3459805439433622ee, type: 3}
  - text: 'The word adobo comes from the Spanish term adobar, meaning to season or
      marinate. '
    characterSprite: {fileID: -511706578061346315, guid: ae71825725b21a3459805439433622ee, type: 3}
  - text: 'However, Filipinos may have already been cooking meat with vinegar before
      Spanish colonization. '
    characterSprite: {fileID: -511706578061346315, guid: ae71825725b21a3459805439433622ee, type: 3}
  - text: With the Spanish term later used to describe the method.
    characterSprite: {fileID: -511706578061346315, guid: ae71825725b21a3459805439433622ee, type: 3}
  - text: 'Pork Adobo is typically simmered with vinegar, soy sauce, garlic, peppercorns,
      and bay leaves. '
    characterSprite: {fileID: -511706578061346315, guid: ae71825725b21a3459805439433622ee, type: 3}
  - text: Every household has its own version, whether the sauce is tangy and plentiful
      or reduced until the meat is nearly dry.
    characterSprite: {fileID: -511706578061346315, guid: ae71825725b21a3459805439433622ee, type: 3}
  - text: Did you know?
    characterSprite: {fileID: -8056027616224820867, guid: 783feefcd5809a142b7b39ffbbe1c917, type: 3}
  - text: 'Adobo has no single recipe that every Filipino household follows! '
    characterSprite: {fileID: -8056027616224820867, guid: 783feefcd5809a142b7b39ffbbe1c917, type: 3}
  - text: Some families prefer more vinegar, while others like their sauce rich and
      savory.
    characterSprite: {fileID: -8056027616224820867, guid: 783feefcd5809a142b7b39ffbbe1c917, type: 3}
  - text: Let's make a dish that tastes like home. Don't forget the garlic!
    characterSprite: {fileID: 0}
